<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paolo Malatesta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1246–c. 1285</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Paolo il Bello</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paolo Malatesta, called il Bello, was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malatesta-da-verucchio">Malatesta da Verucchio</a>, lord of Rimini, and served as captain of the people in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> in 1282. His love affair with his sister-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesca-da-rimini">Francesca da Polenta</a> ended when his brother Giovanni, called Gianciotto, killed them both around 1285. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri">Dante</a> immortalised the pair in the fifth canto of the Inferno.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paolo-malatesta.jpg" alt="Paolo Malatesta" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ernst Klimt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ernst_Klimt_-_Francesca_da_Rimini_e_Paolo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
